rebar explain plan` for the authoring guidance.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State the exact score-normalization formula (input raw bm25, output 0-1) in the Ranking section, including its behavior for a single-result set.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.534,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'score is computed per query and normalized to 0–1, 1 most relevant: raw bm25 is negative and ranks ascending'","The ACs 'Every score lies in 0..1' and 'top-ranked result holds the maximum score' are satisfiable by ANY monotonic-decreasing map, so no AC pins the formula","A derived metric with no computation protocol is an E2 signal (1)/(2) data-design ambiguity"],"finding":"The score normalization from raw bm25 to the 0-1 interval has no stated computation formula; the plan says only 'computed per query and normalized to 0-1, 1 most relevant' but does not specify the mapping (e.g. min-max over the result set, a sigmoid, or 1/(1+|bm25|)).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f004c91ec547a768c","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach > Ranking: 'score is computed per query and normalized to 0-1'","norm_id":"n53050c3746cb972a","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor picks a per-result-set min-max normalization where the single-result case yields a degenerate 0 or 1","A consumer relies on absolute score comparability across queries, which min-max breaks"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify the mapping, e.g. 'score = 1/(1+max(0,-bm25))' (stable per-row, no cross-result dependency), and note it is intra-query relative only.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.85,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State explicitly that this leaf delivers only the DEGRADED/substrate lexical tier of the epic's adopted `vector` architecture (62dc AC1 / ADR 0122), and cite the sibling ticket (by id / dependency) that delivers the vector ranking, so the leaf is demonstrably a faithful subset rather than a substitution; reconcile the provider-unset AC with the parent's 'lexical-only with a diagnostic' degraded-path framing.","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6929,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent epic 62dc operator framing (2026-09-06): 'This is a vector search problem over summaries of large tickets. A lexical-only local index is insufficient and provably so against the historical corpus.'","Parent epic 62dc failure-disposition constraint: the suggestion field 'comes back empty or lexical-only with a diagnostic' — the lexical tier is the DEGRADED path, carrying a diagnostic, not a standalone primary answer.","Leaf names no sibling ticket id or dependency for the embedding tier: 'Siblings add the embedding ranking, the create advisory, and the ADR amendments.'","Leaf AC asserts a plain 'non-empty ranked result' with providers unset and no diagnostic, whereas the parent frames provider-absent service as a diagnostic-bearing degraded tier.","Narrowing to the lexical substrate is legitimate under the epic's degradation contract IF a named sibling delivers vector; absent that naming the subset relation is unestablished — hence incomplete_enumeration, not a floor kind."],"finding":"The leaf delivers a provider-free lexical (fts5) index and defers the adopted `vector` ranking to unnamed 'Siblings', without citing or depending on the sibling that delivers it, so the plan does not establish that the parent epic's adopted vector tier (62dc AC1 / ADR 0122) is delivered anywhere — leaving the lexical-only leaf readable as a substitution for, rather than the degraded substrate beneath, the adopted architecture the epic's operator framing calls 'insufficient and provably so'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fce6fea40bf99352b","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan 'Context / Problem' ('Siblings add the embedding ranking, the create advisory, and the ADR amendments') and AC 'With every model-provider credential environment variable unset, a query returns a non-empty ranked result'","norm_id":"n970aa30309e6478f","priority":0.1571,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer of a later sibling cannot trace which ticket delivers the adopted vector ranking the epic's AC2/AC4 presume.","A reader takes the leaf's provider-unset 'non-empty ranked result' AC as the feature's intended steady-state answer rather than its degraded fallback."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a sentence naming the sibling embedding-tier ticket id and a depends_on/relates_to link, framing this leaf as the lexical substrate of the adopted vector architecture; and note that the provider-unset non-empty result is the epic's degraded tier.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Clarify whether the enumerate+diff is recomputed inside the BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction (under the write lock) so the 'loser's work is redone, not merged' guarantee actually holds, rather than applying a diff computed before the lock was acquired.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3947,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan: 'Concurrent reconcilers serialize on sqlite's write lock; a loser's work is redone, not merged, since each recomputes the hashes it writes.'","compute_dir_hash is a pre-write stat-based hash; nothing in the plan forces the enumerate+diff to run inside the same BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction as the write","The integrity/returnable ACs observe the end state but do not exercise a stale-diff interleaving where the loser's diff predates the winner's commit"],"finding":"The concurrency narrative claims 'a loser's work is redone, not merged, since each recomputes the hashes it writes', but the diff (enumerate + hash-compare against the persisted map) is computed before BEGIN IMMEDIATE acquires the write lock. A reconciler blocked on the lock applies a diff computed against the pre-commit map; the plan does not state the diff is recomputed under the lock, so the 'redone not merged' guarantee is asserted rather than shown.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f35fbc4065161eb84","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Applying the diff ('Concurrent reconcilers serialize on sqlite's write lock; a loser's work is redone, not merged')","norm_id":"n49ed1aff252424de","priority":0.2053,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two creates reconcile near-simultaneously; the blocked one applies a diff built against the map before the winner committed its row"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the plan handles a sqlite build lacking the FTS5 compile-time module (detect at open and surface/log distinctly, or document the FTS5 requirement), so the 'works in every installation' claim holds or is scoped.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan: 'sqlite FTS5 over title and description, bm25 weights title 5.0 / description 1.0'","Plan goal: 'retrieval works in every installation'","FTS5 is a compile-time sqlite option; resolve_symbol confirms the sqlite3 module exists but not that the linked sqlite was built with FTS5 enabled","The failure-disposition section swallows failures to empty results, which would silently mask a missing-FTS5 build as permanent empty results rather than a diagnosable error — contradicting the 'works in every installation' promise"],"finding":"The plan's fitness-for-purpose claim is that lexical retrieval 'works in every installation' with no provider/network, but it does not confirm the FTS5 extension is available. FTS5 is a compile-time option in sqlite and is not guaranteed present in every Python/sqlite build; if absent, 'CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE ... USING fts5' raises and the whole index becomes unbuildable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa924835efe506694","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Ranking ('sqlite FTS5 over title and description') and Context ('retrieval works in every installation')","norm_id":"n4dd058e187b01941","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A Python interpreter wh